# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for tests/run.sh SAN=thread (milestone 5). FFmpeg's libraries are not instrumented: the frame
# threads of its software decoders (H.264 with threads=2) hand frames over with their own synchronisation, which TSAN
# cannot see, so a frame buffer allocated (memset) on a decoder thread and read on the movie thread is reported as a
# race. Only reports with a frame inside FFmpeg's libraries are suppressed; VHS's own code stays checked.
race:libavcodec.so
race:libavutil.so
race:libavformat.so
